  "answer": "This feature has been requested before, so your ticket is a duplicate. The closest match is PowerToys#21313, which asks for a utility that temporarily disables the keyboard, mouse and touchscreen so you can clean them. PowerToys#33581 was closed as a duplicate of #21313. PowerToys#31856 asks for a keyboard and touchscreen lock toggle, and PowerToys#44783 was closed as a duplicate of #31856. #31856 was itself closed as a duplicate of #15427, which is about a shortcut to toggle input devices on and off. In #21313 a maintainer said in 2024 that there were no plans to build this into PowerToys. I found no keyboard lock feature that has shipped. Add a thumbs-up to #21313 instead of opening a new request. Until something ships, one workaround from the tickets is to disable the laptop keyboard in Device Manager (Win+X, then Device Manager, then Keyboards, then Disable). Re-enable it when you finish. Some tickets also mention third-party keyboard-cleaning or locker tools, such as the KeyboardCleanTool at folivora.ai."
 },
